And we think that somehow
we should just be able

00:11:20.866 --> 00:11:25.033
to turn on that eagerness
and turn on that passion.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.663
But we can't.

00:11:31.999 --> 00:11:35.649
'Cause you just can't turn
on passion, you can't just

00:11:35.649 --> 00:11:38.732
turn on the desire to execute a task.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.901
It just doesn't work that way.

00:11:44.901 --> 00:11:48.984
And honestly that isn't
even what motivate means.

00:11:51.561 --> 00:11:53.567
Motivate doesn't mean to yell and scream

00:11:53.567 --> 00:11:54.734
and encourage.

00:11:59.484 --> 00:12:03.651
No, to motivate actually
means to provide a motive,

00:12:05.465 --> 00:12:06.548
a reason why.

00:12:10.513 --> 00:12:14.682
So to motivate someone
is to explain to them why

00:12:14.682 --> 00:12:19.004
they're doing what they're
doing, how it will help them,

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:20.168
where it'll take 'em.

00:12:20.168 --> 00:12:23.068
Why they should continue
to work and to struggle

00:12:23.068 --> 00:12:24.151
and to fight.

00:12:28.558 --> 00:12:32.275
And when you need motivation yourself,

00:12:32.275 --> 00:12:35.364
don't look for someone to scream and yell,

00:12:35.364 --> 00:12:39.531
don't look for someone else
to give you motivation,

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.097
look at yourself.

00:12:46.093 --> 00:12:49.593
Look at yourself, and remind yourself why.

00:12:52.724 --> 00:12:55.807
Why you are doing what you are doing.

00:12:56.988 --> 00:13:01.155
Remind yourself that this
struggle, this temporary pain,

00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:09.179
this fight, this fight that
you're in, this is what

00:13:09.179 --> 00:13:13.346
will make you stronger and
faster and smarter and better.

00:13:21.203 --> 00:13:25.370
And then with that motivation,
go forward into the fray,

00:13:31.142 --> 00:13:34.725
into the storm, into
the heat of the battle

00:13:41.405 --> 00:13:43.405
where victory is forged.

00:13:45.666 --> 00:13:49.249
(soft inspirational music)

00:16:07.438 --> 00:16:11.021
(soft inspirational music)

00:16:11.974 --> 00:16:15.743
- My intention in creating
Master Class came from

00:16:15.743 --> 00:16:20.199
the understanding that
everybody's story is the same.

00:16:20.199 --> 00:16:22.518
All stories are connected.

00:16:22.518 --> 00:16:26.344
And there is nothing that
anyone who's living on Earth

00:16:26.344 --> 00:16:31.143
has ever felt or known or
experienced on a soul level

00:16:31.143 --> 00:16:34.553
that hasn't been felt
or known or experienced

00:16:34.553 --> 00:16:36.098
by someone else.

00:16:36.098 --> 00:16:38.435
One of the most difficult
things in life is feeling

00:16:38.435 --> 00:16:42.342
that you are the only
one, you are the only one

00:16:42.342 --> 00:16:44.974
who's traveled this path,
who's felt this way.

00:16:44.974 --> 00:16:47.260
- I had nowhere to go, I
was homeless at the time,

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:48.834
I'd lost my family.

00:16:48.834 --> 00:16:50.591
Next thing I know, I'm in
this car for three years,

00:16:50.591 --> 00:16:52.560
man, I'm struggling.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:56.911
- Who's experienced such
devastation or joy or triumph

00:16:56.911 --> 00:17:01.793
or victory, so for me, I
define a master as someone

00:17:01.793 --> 00:17:05.960
who has fully stepped in
and owned the full progress

00:17:10.853 --> 00:17:12.578
and trajectory of their life.

00:17:12.578 --> 00:17:13.581
- Persistence pays off.

00:17:13.581 --> 00:17:14.670
That's lesson one.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.561
- But hearing stories told
from the mouths of people

00:17:16.561 --> 00:17:20.728
who know how to live, how
to course-correct, how to

00:17:21.596 --> 00:17:25.700
keep going, how to never
quit, how to rejoice

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:29.688
in the good times, and
have faith in the bad,

00:17:29.688 --> 00:17:31.648
those people are masters.

00:17:31.648 --> 00:17:33.776
Anyone who can do that is a master.

00:17:33.776 --> 00:17:38.163
And their ability to share
their stories only helps

00:17:38.163 --> 00:17:41.163
the trajectory of others who listen.

00:17:42.292 --> 00:17:45.875
(soft inspirational music)

00:17:48.463 --> 00:17:50.556
- So the Instagram Live folks,
if you couldn't hear this,

00:17:50.556 --> 00:17:53.117
he was asking about concert photography,

00:17:53.117 --> 00:17:54.835
how do I get started?

00:17:54.835 --> 00:17:57.787
How do I have a relationship
with these folks?

00:17:57.787 --> 00:17:59.224
Start small.

00:17:59.224 --> 00:18:00.539
But start.

00:18:00.539 --> 00:18:02.625
Like, all this pontificating,
wondering, like, do you

00:18:02.625 --> 00:18:03.854
have a camera?

00:18:03.854 --> 00:18:04.851
Are you going to a show?

00:18:04.851 --> 00:18:08.069
I don't care if you're buying
a ticket, a $9, $10 ticket

00:18:08.069 --> 00:18:10.837
to go to the local show, you
need to start taking pictures,

00:18:10.837 --> 00:18:12.668
because the area that you're
talking about working in

00:18:12.668 --> 00:18:14.839
is very specialized,
it's hard to break into,

00:18:14.839 --> 00:18:16.481
it's hard to make real money.

00:18:16.481 --> 00:18:19.137
And I'm just setting
these things up for you,

00:18:19.137 --> 00:18:21.499
this is the reality of this situation that

00:18:21.499 --> 00:18:23.096
you're asking me to do.

00:18:23.096 --> 00:18:24.346
I don't know if you want to make a living

00:18:24.346 --> 00:18:26.222
and a life doing this stuff,
or if this is a hobby,

00:18:26.222 --> 00:18:28.613
but it's very hard to
break into, and it's very

00:18:28.613 --> 00:18:30.241
hard to make money.

00:18:30.241 --> 00:18:32.324
I want that to cue one
of two things in you.

00:18:32.324 --> 00:18:34.327
You either go well, I don't
give a sh--, this is the thing

00:18:34.327 --> 00:18:35.160
I'm doing.

00:18:36.517 --> 00:18:38.547
I want to do this more than anything,

00:18:38.547 --> 00:18:39.573
and I'm going to do what it takes.

00:18:39.573 --> 00:18:41.120
And if it's hard, that's
awesome, because there's

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.431
going to be less competition.

00:18:42.431 --> 00:18:44.542
Thing two would be like,
oh my God, Chase says it's

00:18:44.542 --> 00:18:46.683
hard to make money and break
in, I don't want to do that.

00:18:46.683 --> 00:18:48.511
If Chase says it's hard, it's really hard.

00:18:48.511 --> 00:18:50.013
Great, then don't do something...

00:18:50.013 --> 00:18:51.795
Go do something else because
you didn't really want it

00:18:51.795 --> 00:18:52.795
bad enough.

00:18:52.795 --> 00:18:54.097
Let's pretend you're in the first camp.

00:18:54.097 --> 00:18:55.094
You want it.

00:18:55.094 --> 00:18:56.134
You're like I don't care,
I'm going to do this.

00:18:56.134 --> 00:18:58.174
This is my calling in life.

00:18:58.174 --> 00:19:00.642
If that's the case, start small.

00:19:00.642 --> 00:19:04.324
Start taking pictures, buy the $10 ticket,

00:19:04.324 --> 00:19:06.166
work your ass to the front
of the row, the thing,

00:19:06.166 --> 00:19:08.464
you're getting smashed in,
you're taking those photographs.

00:19:08.464 --> 00:19:11.065
What can you do to a,
get great at your craft,

00:19:11.065 --> 00:19:13.148
b, go there all the time.

00:19:14.356 --> 00:19:16.225
Not just on the Friday
and Saturday night shows,

00:19:16.225 --> 00:19:18.461
shoot all of the shows,
because you got to put in time

00:19:18.461 --> 00:19:20.211
to master your craft.

00:19:21.072 --> 00:19:23.180
If you're just another
sort of low to medium level

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.041
concert photographer, no
money, no game, it's not

00:19:26.041 --> 00:19:27.488
going to happen for you.

00:19:27.488 --> 00:19:29.589
It might be fun, and you
might be able to get a couple

00:19:29.589 --> 00:19:33.479
of free shows out of the
deal, but I'm not assuming

00:19:33.479 --> 00:19:34.476
that that's your goal.

00:19:34.476 --> 00:19:35.495
I'm assuming that you want to be the best.

00:19:35.495 --> 00:19:37.108
And I could be wrong, so take
this with a grain of salt.

00:19:37.108 --> 00:19:39.814
But if you want to be
the best, you have to...

00:19:39.814 --> 00:19:43.556
How are you then so known that
the first club that you...

00:19:43.556 --> 00:19:47.799
Do you know the owners, do
you know the sound guys,

00:19:47.799 --> 00:19:48.942
do you know the bands that are coming?

00:19:48.942 --> 00:19:49.958
How into it are you?

00:19:49.958 --> 00:19:51.357
Are you doing the other 50%?

00:19:51.357 --> 00:19:55.635
This fricking thing comes
up in every single episode,

00:19:55.635 --> 00:19:57.282
this video that I put
out called The Other 50%.

00:19:57.282 --> 00:19:58.309
You should watch that.

00:19:58.309 --> 00:19:59.761
Are you doing the other 50%?

00:19:59.761 --> 00:20:02.048
Then, go beyond that one club.

00:20:02.048 --> 00:20:07.004
Are you the guy who's known,
like, oh man, I got...

00:20:07.004 --> 00:20:10.873
The Pixies are comin', I
want Xavier to shoot it.

00:20:10.873 --> 00:20:11.938
You have to become that guy.

00:20:11.938 --> 00:20:14.485
And the way you do it is
you're there all the time.

00:20:14.485 --> 00:20:16.500
Just showing up, you've
heard that just showing up

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.105
is half the game.

00:20:18.105 --> 00:20:19.921
You have to have talent,
you have to be skilled,

00:20:19.921 --> 00:20:22.162
you have to have all those
things, but just being

00:20:22.162 --> 00:20:24.099
so relentless with your
pursuit of the thing

00:20:24.099 --> 00:20:25.266
is incredible.

00:20:27.989 --> 00:20:31.572
(soft inspirational music)

00:20:32.548 --> 00:20:33.881
- I am the king!

00:20:35.131 --> 00:20:36.533
I will punish you.

00:20:36.533 --> 00:20:40.794
- Any man who must say "I am
the king" is no true king.

00:20:40.794 --> 00:20:42.163
- [Charlie] This is the
most important sentence

00:20:42.163 --> 00:20:43.755
that Tywin ever says.

00:20:43.755 --> 00:20:46.248
According to Tywin, power
does not come from telling

00:20:46.248 --> 00:20:49.877
other people that you have it,
it comes from showing them.

00:20:49.877 --> 00:20:51.879
Tywin does that in many
ways, and I want to start

00:20:51.879 --> 00:20:54.507
with some of the
sub-communications of power,

00:20:54.507 --> 00:20:56.330
meaning the things that
Tywin does with his

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.778
body language and his voice.

00:20:57.778 --> 00:21:00.013
And I have to give Charles
Dance here, massive amounts

00:21:00.013 --> 00:21:03.248
of credit, because he did
a phenomenal job of acting

00:21:03.248 --> 00:21:04.448
these scenes out.

00:21:04.448 --> 00:21:06.317
So let's explore how Tywin
enters crowded conversations,

00:21:06.317 --> 00:21:08.338
first off, with a boom.

00:21:08.338 --> 00:21:10.247
- I'm told we still have his sisters.

00:21:10.247 --> 00:21:12.646
- The first order of business
is ransoming Sir Jaime.

00:21:12.646 --> 00:21:14.932
- [Council Member] No truces,
we can't afford to look weak.

00:21:14.932 --> 00:21:16.457
- [Council Member] We should
march on them at once.

00:21:16.457 --> 00:21:18.472
- [Council Member] First, we
must return to Casterly Rock

00:21:18.472 --> 00:21:19.504
to raise more...

00:21:19.504 --> 00:21:21.349
- They have my son!

00:21:21.349 --> 00:21:23.102
- [Charlie] Now you may
struggle to be heard when

00:21:23.102 --> 00:21:24.600
there's a lot of people
speaking, many of us do.

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.904
You might stop and start,
try to find your way in

00:21:26.904 --> 00:21:29.012
politely and ultimately
not get listened to at all.

00:21:29.012 --> 00:21:30.268
But not Tywin.

00:21:30.268 --> 00:21:32.734
He startles people by going
from silent to booming

00:21:32.734 --> 00:21:34.620
in an instant.

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:36.608
That grabs attention immediately.

00:21:36.608 --> 00:21:38.629
But what's interesting is
that he often doesn't stay

00:21:38.629 --> 00:21:40.160
booming for too long.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.825
Once he has attention, he
quiets right back down.

00:21:42.825 --> 00:21:45.129
This makes his quiet mode
of interaction just as

00:21:45.129 --> 00:21:48.088
frightening as his booming
tone, because you never know

00:21:48.088 --> 00:21:49.845
when he's going to switch.

00:21:49.845 --> 00:21:51.428
- They have my son!

00:21:55.258 --> 00:21:56.925
Get out, all of you.

00:21:58.331 --> 00:21:59.866
- [Charlie] You don't need
to scream like Tywin does,

00:21:59.866 --> 00:22:01.890
but the lesson of entering
with a slightly louder

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:03.865
and deeper tone is one
that applies just as well

00:22:03.865 --> 00:22:06.254
to modern-day interactions.

00:22:06.254 --> 00:22:07.894
Pay attention to any group
and you'll see that the

00:22:07.894 --> 00:22:10.380
person who is listened to
when there's a lot of people

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:13.174
trying to speak is often
the loudest when entering.

00:22:13.174 --> 00:22:15.068
Don't stay loud forever,
though, if you're going to

00:22:15.068 --> 00:22:16.938
use this small piece of advice,

00:22:16.938 --> 00:22:19.188
because that can just be obnoxious.

00:22:19.188 --> 00:22:20.816
You may also have noticed
that Tywin is very comfortable

00:22:20.816 --> 00:22:21.899
with silence.

00:22:23.243 --> 00:22:25.283
This is a power move that I
discussed in another video,

00:22:25.283 --> 00:22:27.057
so I won't spend too long on
it, and I'll link to it here

00:22:27.057 --> 00:22:29.660
if you want to click the little
white button in the corner,

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:31.789
but Tywin likes to use
silence right after people

00:22:31.789 --> 00:22:34.918
have said something to provoke him.

00:22:34.918 --> 00:22:36.889
It gives them a few extra
seconds to regret their

00:22:36.889 --> 00:22:39.343
decision to stand up to
him, and to sit in fear of

00:22:39.343 --> 00:22:41.248
what he might do next.

00:22:41.248 --> 00:22:43.387
- My father won the real war.

00:22:43.387 --> 00:22:45.964
He killed Prince Rhaegar,
he took the crown,

00:22:45.964 --> 00:22:48.797
while you hid under Casterly Rock.

00:23:01.377 --> 00:23:05.112
- The king is tired,
see him to his chambers.

00:23:05.112 --> 00:23:06.556
- [Charlie] The silence
that Tywin makes creates

00:23:06.556 --> 00:23:08.427
a staredown like you might see for boxing

00:23:08.427 --> 00:23:09.548
or UFC promotions.

00:23:09.548 --> 00:23:12.658
The first person to
flinch or look away loses,

00:23:12.658 --> 00:23:14.583
which is why fighters
go to such great lengths

00:23:14.583 --> 00:23:16.584
to not give an inch of ground.

00:23:16.584 --> 00:23:18.181
And this isn't just an
arbitrary rule that was

00:23:18.181 --> 00:23:19.546
made up for boxing.

00:23:19.546 --> 00:23:21.860
Flinching and breaking
eye contact are built in

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:24.245
evolutionary tells that communicate fear,

00:23:24.245 --> 00:23:26.706
which is why they can
sometimes matter even more

00:23:26.706 --> 00:23:28.986
than raw strength when it
comes to a confrontation.

00:23:28.986 --> 00:23:31.115
Because when one animal
isn't afraid, that's a good

00:23:31.115 --> 00:23:34.709
sign that it has an advantage
that needs to be respected.

00:23:34.709 --> 00:23:36.771
Just watch this charging
gorilla back off when a

00:23:36.771 --> 00:23:39.036
puny little human doesn't
flinch, even though the

00:23:39.036 --> 00:23:42.651
gorilla could obviously
tear him limb from limb.

00:23:42.651 --> 00:23:46.929
- [Man] He charged and
charged and charged again,

00:23:46.929 --> 00:23:48.873
and I think, and I'm sure, if I would have

00:23:48.873 --> 00:23:51.091
even flinched once....

00:23:51.091 --> 00:23:52.766
- [Charlie] But Tywin's
subcommunications of power

00:23:52.766 --> 00:23:53.939
go beyond the ape realm.

00:23:53.939 --> 00:23:56.652
His word choice is a distinctly
human way of using power.

00:23:56.652 --> 00:23:58.808
He doesn't ask people
what to do or make threats

00:23:58.808 --> 00:24:00.933
by saying if you do this,
then I'm going to respond

00:24:00.933 --> 00:24:02.001
like this.

00:24:02.001 --> 00:24:04.084
He tells people what they
are going to do, using the

00:24:04.084 --> 00:24:04.917
word will.

00:24:05.754 --> 00:24:07.878
It conveys absolutely
certainty that they will do

00:24:07.878 --> 00:24:10.449
as they are told, and
again, the certainty that

00:24:10.449 --> 00:24:13.069
Tywin will be listened
to adds to the sense

00:24:13.069 --> 00:24:14.736
that he should be listened to.

00:24:14.736 --> 00:24:18.319
(soft inspirational music)

00:24:20.601 --> 00:24:22.154
- Taking action is a cure-all.

00:24:22.154 --> 00:24:24.347
Taking action solves all
the problems that you're

00:24:24.347 --> 00:24:25.625
going through.

00:24:25.625 --> 00:24:27.411
Whatever problem you have,
whatever thing is in front

00:24:27.411 --> 00:24:28.945
of you, whatever obstacle
is there that seems

00:24:28.945 --> 00:24:32.144
unsurmountable, it's not
going to get fixed by just

00:24:32.144 --> 00:24:34.971
sitting and complaining
and wallowing and feeling

00:24:34.971 --> 00:24:36.952
sorry for yourself.

00:24:36.952 --> 00:24:39.334
It happens from taking action.

00:24:39.334 --> 00:24:41.192
As soon as you can move
from that place of being

00:24:41.192 --> 00:24:45.770
unhappy and desperate,
and sorry for yourself to

00:24:45.770 --> 00:24:47.437
how do I solve this?

00:24:48.323 --> 00:24:50.109
Who do I need to contact to help me?

00:24:50.109 --> 00:24:53.047
How can I use the resources
I have to fix this?

00:24:53.047 --> 00:24:54.560
As soon as you start moving to that land,

00:24:54.560 --> 00:24:56.680
that's when you start to make progress.

00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:58.581
Taking action is the cure-all.

00:24:58.581 --> 00:25:00.747
And this is what happens so
many times to entrepreneurs,

00:25:00.747 --> 00:25:03.890
not even just with problems
but with ideas in general.

00:25:03.890 --> 00:25:05.812
How often do you get an
idea for something that

00:25:05.812 --> 00:25:08.739
you want to do, and then
you say tomorrow I'm

00:25:08.739 --> 00:25:10.690
going to do it, and then tomorrow
comes and you don't do it?

00:25:10.690 --> 00:25:12.334
How many times?

00:25:12.334 --> 00:25:15.099
That happens over and over
and over and over and again.

00:25:15.099 --> 00:25:17.500
It's a human condition,
it's not just entrepreneurs.

00:25:17.500 --> 00:25:19.408
We have these things, these
ambitions, these drives

00:25:19.408 --> 00:25:21.322
that we set for ourselves
and then we don't follow

00:25:21.322 --> 00:25:22.509
through on.

00:25:22.509 --> 00:25:26.078
The best way to start
on that idea you have

00:25:26.078 --> 00:25:27.403
is to take action.

00:25:27.403 --> 00:25:28.611
Do something immediately.

00:25:28.611 --> 00:25:29.981
As soon as you set a goal, I want to

00:25:29.981 --> 00:25:31.360
start a YouTube channel.

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:32.378
Great.

00:25:32.378 --> 00:25:33.411
What are you going to do
on your YouTube channel?

00:25:33.411 --> 00:25:34.564
I want to interview people.

00:25:34.564 --> 00:25:36.057
Amazing.

00:25:36.057 --> 00:25:37.946
Today, set up your YouTube channel,

00:25:37.946 --> 00:25:40.130
and send out 10 emails
to people to ask them

00:25:40.130 --> 00:25:41.507
for interviews.

00:25:41.507 --> 00:25:43.415
People that you know, people
that you think will say yes.

00:25:43.415 --> 00:25:45.479
When you commit to somebody
else, you're much more

00:25:45.479 --> 00:25:46.785
likely to follow through.

00:25:46.785 --> 00:25:49.459
And what happens is,
perfection becomes the enemy

00:25:49.459 --> 00:25:50.292
of action.

00:25:51.325 --> 00:25:53.634
You want to make it perfect,
and because you make it

00:25:53.634 --> 00:25:57.840
perfect, it gets more, more,
more, more, more complex

00:25:57.840 --> 00:26:01.721
and complexion is the enemy of execution,

00:26:01.721 --> 00:26:04.157
because you build it up to this big thing,

00:26:04.157 --> 00:26:05.924
this big scary thing
that has to be perfect,

00:26:05.924 --> 00:26:07.749
you don't do anything.

00:26:07.749 --> 00:26:09.414
Before I set up my YouTube
channel, I need to have

00:26:09.414 --> 00:26:11.495
the perfect channel art,
or I need to have the

00:26:11.495 --> 00:26:13.657
right thumbnails, and I
need to know what my script

00:26:13.657 --> 00:26:16.016
is going to be, and I need
to know my intro and opener

00:26:16.016 --> 00:26:18.152
and I need the gear, and
all of these things that

00:26:18.152 --> 00:26:19.869
you need to have to make a perfect video.

00:26:19.869 --> 00:26:21.925
And because it becomes this big thing,

00:26:21.925 --> 00:26:23.521
you don't do anything about it.

00:26:23.521 --> 00:26:26.709
And then the next day you
wake up, and it's gone, poof.

00:26:26.709 --> 00:26:30.391
As soon as you set a goal for yourself,

00:26:30.391 --> 00:26:32.474
I want to go and do this,

00:26:34.047 --> 00:26:36.390
the best next thing you can do is

00:26:36.390 --> 00:26:39.835
take some form of immediate action,

00:26:39.835 --> 00:26:42.558
and ideally, commit to somebody else,

00:26:42.558 --> 00:26:45.777
whether it's a friend,
whether it's a potential

00:26:45.777 --> 00:26:48.299
customer, whether you're
sending emails out,

00:26:48.299 --> 00:26:50.326
whether it's your family,
whether it's a neighbor,

00:26:50.326 --> 00:26:53.107
commit to somebody else,
because when you do that,

00:26:53.107 --> 00:26:55.857
you're much more likely to follow through,

00:26:55.857 --> 00:26:59.245
because you won't let them down.

00:26:59.245 --> 00:27:01.240
You'll let yourself down all the time.

00:27:01.240 --> 00:27:02.439
You let yourself down
every morning when you wake

00:27:02.439 --> 00:27:03.455
up and hit the snooze button.

00:27:03.455 --> 00:27:04.525
You're letting yourself down.

00:27:04.525 --> 00:27:06.159
The first thing you do in the
morning is let yourself down.

00:27:06.159 --> 00:27:08.974
You set a goal, boom, I let myself down.

00:27:08.974 --> 00:27:10.586
You let yourself down all the time.

00:27:10.586 --> 00:27:13.481
But you won't let other
people down nearly as much.

00:27:13.481 --> 00:27:17.224
So take immediate action,
and then follow through

00:27:17.224 --> 00:27:19.379
with somebody else, so that you don't let

00:27:19.379 --> 00:27:21.296
yourself and them down.

00:27:22.291 --> 00:27:23.302
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:27:23.302 --> 00:27:24.921
I hope you enjoyed.

